WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.856 --> 00:00:03.816
On the MES in hall B there is an order.

2
00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:08.060
The filling unit of line 3 fills cartons from the tank.

3
00:00:09.086 --> 00:00:11.292
What happens between that order and the machine?

4
00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:14.261
You are the engineer and find out.

5
00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:19.416
ISA-95 describes how a plant’s systems fit together,

6
00:00:19.531 --> 00:00:21.632
from the machine up to the business system.

7
00:00:22.645 --> 00:00:24.352
Four topics follow that chain.

8
00:00:25.061 --> 00:00:27.128
First the levels and the systems.

9
00:00:28.164 --> 00:00:31.972
Then how they talk, where data is kept and who looks after them.

10
00:00:33.258 --> 00:00:36.880
The first topic is ISA-95 and the Purdue model.

11
00:00:37.593 --> 00:00:40.530
Every system belongs on one of five levels.

12
00:00:41.524 --> 00:00:46.667
The photo eye at the belt is level 1 and the PLC in the cabinet level 2.

13
00:00:47.668 --> 00:00:51.267
The MES is level 3 and the ERP level 4.

14
00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:56.892
You draw the information flow between the MES and the ERP.

15
00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:02.092
The second topic is PLC, SCADA, MES and ERP.

16
00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.733
One order runs through all four.

17
00:01:05.775 --> 00:01:08.341
The ERP knows what the customer wants.

18
00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:14.182
The MES spreads the work, SCADA monitors and the PLC runs the machine.

19
00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:19.631
An order goes down to the PLC through the cable and the network cabinet.

20
00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:22.732
The count goes up to the MES.

21
00:01:23.763 --> 00:01:27.583
You follow the production order from the ERP to the PLC.

22
00:01:28.824 --> 00:01:32.946
The third topic is OPC UA, MQTT and the historian.

23
00:01:33.643 --> 00:01:35.861
Systems talk in agreed languages.

24
00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:39.643
OPC UA is a standard for machine data.

25
00:01:40.354 --> 00:01:43.257
MQTT is a lightweight messaging protocol.

26
00:01:44.242 --> 00:01:48.271
The historian keeps measurements for years and shows them as a trend.

27
00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:51.930
You set up an OPC server and tags.

28
00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.005
The fourth topic is IT-OT convergence.

29
00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:00.190
Office IT and the technology on the floor grow together.

30
00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:02.452
Who looks after what?

31
00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:07.008
IT runs network and servers, automation the PLC.

32
00:02:08.001 --> 00:02:11.623
You call in the machine builder, as it supplies the controls.

33
00:02:12.692 --> 00:02:17.313
Then the order reaches the unit and the count goes back to the MES.

34
00:02:18.599 --> 00:02:19.388
The whole map.

35
00:02:20.115 --> 00:02:23.494
This is the second station of Automation and IT.

36
00:02:24.486 --> 00:02:26.193
Every topic has four levels.

37
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.287
Start with The five levels of ISA-95 at Basics level.

38
00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.121
It shows how everything fits together.

39
00:02:35.168 --> 00:02:38.117
At Working knowledge level come two maps of the plant,

40
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:41.670
orders down, machine data and patching with lifecycles.

41
00:02:42.698 --> 00:02:47.667
At Advanced level come the four operations areas, the link with the MES,

42
00:02:47.853 --> 00:02:49.966
MQTT and change control.

43
00:02:50.998 --> 00:02:56.212
At Expert level come the cloud, judging an interface, the unified namespace.

44
00:02:56.924 --> 00:02:57.992
Also governance.

45
00:02:59.021 --> 00:03:03.166
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
